Package: erhai-firefox
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Section: web
Priority: optional
Description: Firefox from Mozilla's APT repository for the OnePlus Pad 2 Pro
 Ubuntu's firefox package installs the Firefox snap, which renders with the
 graphics libraries of its own snap runtime. Those have no driver for this
 tablet's Adreno 830, and this kernel does not provide the confinement snaps
 expect. This package configures Mozilla's official APT repository
 (packages.mozilla.org) with its signing key and gives Mozilla's firefox
 priority over Ubuntu's transitional package, so Firefox runs with the system
 graphics driver and is updated through APT, unattended upgrades included.
 .
 It does not install Firefox itself. The root filesystem build installs a
 pinned Mozilla build; an existing installation runs "apt update" and
 "apt install firefox" once. With Mozilla's Firefox installed, the Firefox
 snap is removed after snapd has seeded it, unless a user has already started
 it and so keeps a profile under ~/snap/firefox. snapd and the other snaps
 stay. The Ubuntu dock pins Mozilla's Firefox in place of the snap.
